# Copy to .dev.vars for `npm run dev`. In production the key is a Worker
# secret: `npx wrangler secret put DASH_KEY`.
DASH_KEY=local-dev-key
# wrangler dev is plain HTTP; the live desk refuses HTTP unless this is off.
HTTPS_ONLY=off

# Going live from the desk (README, "Going live from the desk"). Without all
# five, /api/golive/* answers 503 golive-not-set-up and the rest of the desk
# works as before. In production each one is a Worker secret too.
# Not CF_API_TOKEN and CF_ACCOUNT_ID: wrangler reads those from your shell as
# its own deploy credentials, so the desk's are named apart.
# The Cloudflare API token that changes the client zones' DNS and Workers:
# GOLIVE_API_TOKEN=
# The Cloudflare account that holds the client zones and their Workers:
# GOLIVE_ACCOUNT_ID=
# The Cloudflare Access team, <team>.cloudflareaccess.com:
# ACCESS_TEAM_DOMAIN=
# The Access application's Audience (AUD) tag:
# ACCESS_AUD=
# Who may go live: email addresses, separated by commas or spaces:
# GOLIVE_EMAILS=
